| YSFlight M1 tests. Started by !Run in a task window.
| Each run's output appears in this window (save it from the window's
| menu). Its error output (stderr: messages, and the crash report with the
| RISC OS error and a backtrace) goes to a file in <YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.
| UnixLib does the 2> redirection; Do expands the <variables> in the
| arguments, which Run alone doesn't. Time prints the clock between steps.
WimpSlot -min 16384K
CDir <YSFlight$Dir>.Logs
Echo YSFlight M1 tests. Each list should take seconds, not minutes.
Time
Echo 1/4 Aircraft list (88)...
Do Run <YSFlight$Dir>.!RunImage -listairplane 2><YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.AircraftE
Time
Echo 2/4 Field list (18)...
Do Run <YSFlight$Dir>.!RunImage -listfield 2><YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.FieldsE
Time
Echo 3/4 Start positions on Aomori (36)...
Do Run <YSFlight$Dir>.!RunImage -liststartpos AOMORI 2><YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.AomoriE
Time
Echo 4/4 Start positions on Hawaii (56)...
Do Run <YSFlight$Dir>.!RunImage -liststartpos HAWAII 2><YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.HawaiiE
Time
Echo Now the server: it loads a map and flies AI traffic, with 4 threads.
Echo After "Ready to go!" leave it a few minutes, then press Escape.
Do Run <YSFlight$Dir>.!RunImage -server pi 2><YSFlight$Dir>.Logs.ServerE
Time
Echo Finished. Please save this window's text and send it with !YSFlight.Logs.
